// Archipelago check reward pool. See docs/goals-and-checks.md "Feature 2" for
// the design and docs/ap-yaml-options.md for the tuning knobs. Static data, one
// row per (category, item) option.
//
// GENERATED by scripts/gen-rewards.py - hand edits are fine but re-running the
// generator overwrites them; prefer editing the generator.
//
// min_level is the level at which the tier becomes RELEVANT, checked against the
// category's governing stat (or %qp for cash). It is no longer a hard gate:
// ~ap_tier_weight turns it into a bias, so you mostly get what you can use, still
// sometimes get a tier or two above you, and rarely get something far out of
// reach. qty/qty_max bound a uniform quantity roll.

// ---- ores (smithing - what CONSUMES the ore, so a smith who never mines
// still gets usable material). Coal is deliberately the fattest stack in the
// table: it is the single biggest bottleneck in a randomized world, where the
// gathering shuffle can take coal rocks away from you entirely. ----
[ap_reward_ores_clay]
table=ap_rewards
data=category,ores
data=min_level,1
data=reward,clay
data=qty,15
data=qty_max,30

[ap_reward_ores_copper_ore]
table=ap_rewards
data=category,ores
data=min_level,1
data=reward,copper_ore
data=qty,20
data=qty_max,40

[ap_reward_ores_tin_ore]
